    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0213" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6–2647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ward</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-26T18:00:00+09:00">June 26, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 26—12:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>110. Nationalist northward drive to relieve Ssupingkai progressing. About 20,000
                    Nationalist combat troops involved. Commonly believed drive will be
                    successful.</p>
                <p>Unless Communists change recent tactics it is believed they will permit
                    northbound Nationalists’ column to extend itself without much resistance until
                    column approaches Ssupingkai, where resistance will probably be stiffened
                    sufficiently to cause Northeast Chinese Command to send reinforcements from
                    Mukden area. If this materializes it can then be expected Communists will
                    institute feint or actual drive on Fushun.</p>
                <p>Absence any damage by Communists to industrial plants during recent occupation
                    Penhsi probably indicates their confidence early permanent reoccupation. No
                    known damage by Communists to plants Antung, which still in their hands. Rail
                    traffic restored Mukden–Yingkow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ward</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
